#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0169 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: The value of CNSR is not a positive integer or 0
#note "Added 2026-09-14 (PLAN-column-type-conformance carried-forward). CNSR is Num in the standard but was measured Char x3 across this corpus's own fixtures (plan §3 Q4), and on a Char column `num(CNSR)` is the conversion ruling R2 restored rather than the identity it is on every other CNSR fixture. Row 1 is a negative integer shipped as text: it fires through `num(CNSR) < 0` only if the conversion happens — with num() still a no-op tag the comparison reads a character cell, gets NaN, and the rule silently stops firing. Row 2 is a conformant 0 as text and must not fire."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 CNSR=-1
#define standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col CNSR type=Char
---
-1
0
---
